  "fitness": "undetermined",
  "outcome": "insufficient_information",
  "explanation": "The assessment is undetermined because the supplied facts do not establish either unconditional clearance or a current restriction sufficient to deny a licence. While the patient has insulin-treated type 2 diabetes and experienced an episode of hypoglycaemia (sweating, confusion) after skipping lunch last week, the timeline for the mandatory six-week non-driving period following a 'severe' event cannot be confirmed without a contemporaneous clinical assessment defining the severity. Furthermore, critical prerequisites for a conditional licence are missing: there is no specialist's opinion on glucose control or awareness, no documented evidence of maintained early warning symptoms (the patient could not organize self-treatment), and insufficient data regarding the specific insulin regimen used. The absence of three months of monitoring records prevents verification of adherence to self-monitoring requirements.","missing_information": ["contemporaneous clinical assessment confirming severity of hypoglycaemic event", "specialist's opinion on glucose control and behaviour over a reasonable interval", "confirmation of maintained early warning symptoms (hypoglycaemia awareness)", "specific insulin preparation and dose details", "three months of continuous glucose monitoring records"]}
